{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetPTCmZQjeVJQLmJi5LX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All tests pass. Let me verify the test count:\n\n**Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` directory\n\n**Result:** 21 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS\n\n**Details:**\n- OrderControllerTest: 11 tests (4 existing + 7 new for cancel functionality)\n- ShipmentControllerTest: 6 tests (5 existing + 1 new for rejection of shipment creation on cancelled order)\n- SampleServiceApplicationTests: 1 test\n- CustomerControllerTest: 3 tests\n\nNo test failures or fixes needed.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. **Existing build passes** ✓ — BUILD SUCCESS with no compilation errors\n2. **Existing tests pass** ✓ — All 21 tests pass, including 9 pre-existing tests\n3. **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's `CREATED` shipments** ✓\n   - Test: `cancels an ACTIVE order and returns the cancelled order` — asserts order status CANCELLED in response and verifies via separate GET\n   - Test: `cancelling an order cancels its CREATED shipments` — verifies CREATED shipment becomes CANCELLED\n4. **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** ✓\n   - Uses `ConflictException` for 409 and `ResourceNotFoundException` for 404, same as existing endpoints\n   - Error codes added to `ErrorCode` enum\n   - Global exception handler converts to standard ApiError envelope\n5. **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a `CONFIRMED` shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** ✓\n   - Test: `cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds and changes nothing` — idempotent retry\n   - Test: `cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment is blocked with 409` — verifies order stays ACTIVE and shipment stays CONFIRMED via separate GETs\n   - Test: `cancelling non-existent order returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND` — 404 error\n   - Test: `rejects shipment creation for a CANCELLED order with 409` — 409 when creating shipment for cancelled order\n6. **No new Maven dependency appears** ✓ — pom.xml unchanged\n7. **No unrelated production file changes** ✓ — only order, shipment, and api package files touched\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order (required; needed for order lifecycle)\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and ORDER_IS_CANCELLED error codes (required; new error cases)\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** — No changes needed (repository pattern sufficient)\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId() method (required; needed to query shipments by orderId for validation)\n5. **OrderController.kt** — Added cancel endpoint and injected ShipmentRepository (required; implements feature)\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders and injected OrderRepository (required; enforces constraint)\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 7 new tests covering all cancel scenarios (required; per skill requirement)\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 new test for rejection on cancelled order (required; per skill requirement)\n\n**Test verification against testing-and-verification skill:**\n\n1. **Does any assertion read a response body?** ✓ — All tests assert `jsonPath` on response bodies (status, orderId, etc.)\n2. **Is there a `get(...)` request that is not the call under test, whose response is asserted on?** ✓ — Multiple tests follow each state-changing POST with a GET:\n   - \"cancels an ACTIVE order\" → POST cancel then GET /orders/{orderId}\n   - \"cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment\" → POST cancel then GET /orders/{orderId} and GET /shipments/{shipmentId}\n   - \"cancelling an order cancels its CREATED shipments\" → POST cancel then GET /shipments/{shipmentId}\n3. **Is there such a `get(...)` after a **refused** call, asserting no change?** ✓\n   - \"cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment is blocked\" → POST cancel (fails), then GET /orders to verify ACTIVE, GET /shipment to verify CONFIRMED\n   - \"rejects shipment creation for a CANCELLED order\" → POST shipment (fails), then GET /orders to verify CANCELLED\n4. **Does a refusal assert `error.code` rather than only the status?** ✓ — Multiple assertions on error.code:\n   - ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED for blocked cancel\n   - ORDER_NOT_FOUND for missing order\n   - ORDER_IS_CANCELLED for shipment creation on cancelled order\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Customers can cancel an order until a carrier accepts a shipment, with idempotent retry support and all-or-nothing validation.\n\nChanged       \n- Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order data class\n- ApiError.kt: Added two new ErrorCode values (ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED, ORDER_IS_CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() method to query shipments by orderId\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with validation and ShipmentRepository injection\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders and OrderRepository injection\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 7 comprehensive tests covering cancel success, idempotent retry, blocked cancel, missing order, and shipment cancellation\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for rejection of shipment creation on cancelled order\n\nTests\n- `creates an order in ACTIVE status` — verifies new orders have ACTIVE status\n- `cancels an ACTIVE order and returns the cancelled order` — verifies POST cancel succeeds, response has CANCELLED status, and state persists via GET\n- `cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds and changes nothing` — verifies idempotent retry succeeds with same response and no state change\n- `cancelling